From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Gazelka <andrew.gazelka@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 18:11:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] libstore/daemon: record client uid and user for the goal
 graph

The daemon accepts connections as root and forks a worker per client,
so only the daemon knows which uid/user a worker is serving. Record it
via `setBuildStatusClientInfo()` right after the fork, so the worker's
goal-graph file can attribute the work to the requesting client.

Refs indexable-inc/index#2485
Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/nix/unix/daemon.cc b/src/nix/unix/daemon.cc
index 5b41d42b3..77499ba26 100644
--- a/src/nix/unix/daemon.cc
+++ b/src/nix/unix/daemon.cc
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include "nix/cmd/legacy.hh"
 #include "nix/cmd/unix-socket-server.hh"
 #include "nix/store/daemon.hh"
+#include "nix/store/build/goal-graph.hh"
 #include "man-pages.hh"
 
 #include <algorithm>
@@ -348,6 +349,10 @@ static void daemonLoop(ref<const StoreConfig> storeConfig, std::optional<Trusted
                             strncpy(savedArgv[1], processName.c_str(), strlen(savedArgv[1]));
                         }
 
+                        // Record the client identity so the worker's goal
+                        // graph can attribute the work to it.
+                        setBuildStatusClientInfo({.uid = peer.uid, .user = userName});
+
                         // Handle the connection.
                         auto store = storeConfig->openStore();
                         store->init();
